WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.737
New Tibet connects Tibetan identity, community and a digital wallet.

00:00:04.737 --> 00:00:10.895
This walkthrough uses the current mobile prototype, a fictional member and simulated tokens.

00:00:10.895 --> 00:00:14.684
Join with a Green Book or Blue Book.

00:00:14.684 --> 00:00:18.000
Book approval earns one hundred Tibet coins.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Registration has two stages.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:24.000
First, choose your book and a display name.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:26.500
You can use a pseudonym.

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:33.000
Then provide four book photographs and a short video with the verification code.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:38.000
These sample documents belong to the fictional applicant Tenzin Dolma.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:41.500
Passport verification and contact details are optional.

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:45.000
Verification information is deleted after sixty days.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:52.761
Once the book application is accepted, the profile displays a membership card with a Q R code.

00:00:52.761 --> 00:01:00.065
The wallet receives one hundred Tibet coins, with a dated signup reward in its activity timeline.

00:01:00.065 --> 00:01:03.717
The wallet notification clears when you open it.

00:01:03.717 --> 00:01:06.000
All balances here are demonstrations.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:09.073
The passport check is an optional upgrade.

00:01:09.073 --> 00:01:16.976
A compatible N F C passport generates a private proof, rather than sending passport details to New Tibet.

00:01:16.976 --> 00:01:20.049
In this recording we simulate that result.

00:01:20.049 --> 00:01:24.000
The enhanced tier adds another one hundred Tibet coins.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:27.304
The ecosystem could reward participation inside partner applications.

00:01:27.304 --> 00:01:32.261
This example gives one hundred Tibet coins for seven consecutive learning days.

00:01:32.261 --> 00:01:36.391
Here we simulate those days in a proposed Monlam campaign.

00:01:36.391 --> 00:01:39.696
The reward appears once in the wallet timeline.

00:01:39.696 --> 00:01:43.000
Partner agreements and real payouts are not enabled.

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:46.538
The planned native messenger uses BitChat's Bluetooth mesh.

00:01:46.538 --> 00:01:51.846
Messages pass from phone to phone, with nearby devices acting as relays.

00:01:51.846 --> 00:01:58.923
There is no central messaging server to censor the Bluetooth route, and internet is not required.

00:01:58.923 --> 00:02:02.904
Delivery depends on nearby phones and can take time.

00:02:02.904 --> 00:02:06.000
This website does not transmit Bluetooth messages.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:08.111
Petitions is restored after Chat.

00:02:08.111 --> 00:02:11.067
Everyone can read proposals and sample results.

00:02:11.067 --> 00:02:14.867
Verified Green Book holders can create and support petitions.

00:02:14.867 --> 00:02:22.044
Ecosystem tiles show possible integrations, alongside a developer guide for Sign in with New Tibet I D.

00:02:22.044 --> 00:02:25.000
These sites are examples, not signed partners.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:31.809
The roadmap has three phases: identity and on ramp, partner utility, then digital nation and culture.

00:02:31.809 --> 00:02:35.638
Future uses include cultural archives, voting and community payments.

00:02:35.638 --> 00:02:40.745
The data policy explains sixty day deletion and optional country level totals.

00:02:40.745 --> 00:02:45.000
Wallet security and optional contacts can be added after registration.
